<!--
  The out-of-call registrar of a caller: every REGISTER gets 200 with the
  expiry of the expires keyword. A UAC run of SIPp gives a REGISTER of the DUT
  to its out-of-call scenario, so the line keeps its binding while the caller
  runs. sipp_uac_start() in run_e2e.sh passes -key expires 3600 on every run.

  The inbound churn flow passes 10. sip_reg_refresh_secs() (src/proto/sip/reg.c)
  takes the lesser of half the expiry and the expiry minus thirty seconds,
  with a fifteen second floor. If that floor is not below the expiry, it
  takes half the expiry with a two second floor instead. The line therefore
  re-registers every five seconds, and a flow that runs longer than that
  carries the refresh traffic of the field capture beside its calls.
-->
<scenario name="REGISTER out-of-call responder">
  <recv request="REGISTER"/>

  <send>
    <![CDATA[
      SIP/2.0 200 OK
      [last_Via:]
      [last_From:]
      [last_To:];tag=sipp-[pid]-register
      [last_Call-ID:]
      [last_CSeq:]
      [last_Contact:]
      Expires: [expires]
      Content-Length: 0

    ]]>
  </send>
</scenario>
